            "review_title": "Review at Roof Garden Restaurant",
            "review_text": "DAMHertfordshire\nHertfordshire, England220 contributions\n0\nGood views, awful food\nJul 2015 • Couples\nWe ate here because it was raining heavily and we were staying in the hotel. \nThe views are great but the restaurant was so dark we couldn't read the menu, a waiter bought a lamp over to us. We ordered spring rolls, chicken in lemongrass and chilli and another chicken dish. The spring rolls tasted awful. They were obviously not fresh and had a rancid taste to them. We were sharing them between the two of us, but ended up leaving a few of them. The chicken with lemongrass arrived and tasted of turmeric with more turmeric. My husbands chicken was supposed to be in a Hoi sin sauce but tasted of nothing. When we questioned if we had the correct meal the waiter went and asked the chef, who informed him that he had run out of lemongrass. I think he decided to substitute it with turmeric. We had no explanation for my husbands chicken. To make up for it, towards the end of the meal, they bought us another plate of spring rolls, which we refused. \nThis meal cost us nearly 900,000 dong for one starter, two main courses and a beer and glass of wine. It was not only the worst meal we had in Vietnam but possibly the worst meal we have ever had. \nTo cap it all a very large group came in and pulled out their own food and drink and received more attention than we did!\nSave your money, get a cab to Cyclo Resto.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 12, 2015",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-10",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
